{"schemaVersion":"1.0.0","kind":"eigenquestions-fine-index","destinations":[{"id":"source-question:ba8bd620a94664cf6e539e4aec242be5fddde7d28b3a8eef856937ccf7d878fa","title":"The desired solution joins two flat asymptotic regions through a nonzero spherical throat. In the displayed scalar-gravity equations, this geometry requires a negative scalar geodesic norm, which real profiles on the original Riemannian target cannot supply.","connectionCount":1,"detail":{"shardId":"destination-details-fine-0002"},"indexTemplate":"source_question"},{"id":"source-question:ba8dc270cd48962a1164bdc12f752075a802969d43badfe5598205fdfc63ad02","title":"The effective O’KKLT model tests thermal volume stabilization while representing metastable supersymmetry breaking by one light uplifting field. One-exponential KKLT and two-exponential racetrack sectors provide the cases compared.","connectionCount":1,"detail":{"shardId":"destination-details-fine-0003"},"indexTemplate":"source_question"},{"id":"source-question:ba2db2d76dd6ce5790bb60ec53801f7a3dcc9b3b31008a748cc4b2135a5fc45f","title":"How strongly does bulk LARGE-volume supersymmetry breaking generate gravity and anomaly mediated soft terms on local Standard Model/GUT branes, and what follows for gauge mediation and the cosmological moduli problem?","connectionCount":1,"detail":{"shardId":"destination-details-fine-0007"},"indexTemplate":"source_question"},{"id":"source-question:baadbe47767db2a8c2527f12286a4ff9de2581f597abeee7c458de70688d76a3","title":"Can angular fluctuations modulate the tachyonic end of radial D-brane inflation, generating curvature perturbations with both local and equilateral bispectra, and does their coexistence predict a distinctive trispectrum component?","connectionCount":1,"detail":{"shardId":"destination-details-fine-0007"},"indexTemplate":"source_question"},{"id":"source-question:babad4506b7b1da33d8a61c1e9b7a24c4625c421b489c6fc5f5b118174a5b831","title":"Which N=4 gauge algebras actually arise from the considered geometric and nongeometric flux compactifications, and can their flux dictionary realize the gaugings then known to possess de Sitter solutions?","connectionCount":1,"detail":{"shardId":"destination-details-fine-0008"},"indexTemplate":"source_question"},{"id":"source-question:ba486b46da7b3b301ba070055d9f0c84c7b38190deee9d3d963da8ec66c2b94c","title":"When does gravitational backreaction change the thin-wall tunnelling exponent, and which scalar potentials admit rapid transitions between perturbatively stable minima?","connectionCount":1,"detail":{"shardId":"destination-details-fine-0011"},"indexTemplate":"source_question"},{"id":"source-question:ba93e9ad729cddee11fbad657cfe0875b4c1f1729fd5c085112b80ef53c69db3","title":"How can the EFT of cosmic acceleration be implemented in CAMB to predict linear cosmological observables for mapped single-scalar theories and parametrized EFT models, while retaining scalar time evolution and checking theoretical viability?","connectionCount":1,"detail":{"shardId":"destination-details-fine-0015"},"indexTemplate":"source_question"},{"id":"source-question:ba3d7cdc36ea0fa1e2cf6349c1bec473a418c6d7bf6c995d8bacb651b0567f73","title":"Can a canonically normalized single-field potential approaching an inflationary plateau by a power law fit the quoted observations, produce distinguishable tensor signals, and admit economical mass scales and supersymmetric toy realizations?","connectionCount":1,"detail":{"shardId":"destination-details-fine-0022"},"indexTemplate":"source_question"},{"id":"source-question:ba9523aca69d1a05f2dd3cf148882e1ad5e9bac5a3353059db103a055f4eec61","title":"Do flux configurations that break supersymmetry below the KK scale supply static backgrounds around which quantum stabilization can be computed, or do higher-derivative corrections instead require rolling solutions and a different treatment of nonperturbative effects?","connectionCount":1,"detail":{"shardId":"destination-details-fine-0026"},"indexTemplate":"source_question"},{"id":"source-question:badec2337c13522ea3f6764cf9f089669d3a5c15d599ca6f1657b05151a5902e","title":"When can complex-structure tuning make a free rational section torsional, enhancing a U(1) to a non-simply-connected gauge group? How does a related bisection geometry with a torsional Jacobian fit the F-theory interpretation?","connectionCount":1,"detail":{"shardId":"destination-details-fine-0026"},"indexTemplate":"source_question"},{"id":"source-question:babbb2a02c04892aff7f659a1626ba51019751d87b6b1e30f8ace64464069bcb","title":"Does a restriction on non-BPS charged objects in flat space also exclude supersymmetry breaking imposed only at an AdS boundary? The paper separates these claims because the boundary condition is absent before the near-horizon limit.","connectionCount":1,"detail":{"shardId":"destination-details-fine-0026"},"indexTemplate":"source_question"},{"id":"source-question:ba76b96a8b428c8f2cc3597403e7e75e05e4567765fabd7d6dbc340bf48cf001","title":"The quintic LG point starts the test deep inside a finite non-geometric region. Its distance to the large-volume chart measures the possible delay before asymptotic mass lightening.","connectionCount":0,"detail":{"shardId":"destination-details-fine-0028"},"indexTemplate":"source_question"},{"id":"source-question:ba36be952db800f85844368f62f94d0a1e603255040787e62c6947183c5367fd","title":"How does dynamically selected brane curvature depend on boundary curvature, and can it be parametrically small in brane Planck units without tuning model parameters?","connectionCount":1,"detail":{"shardId":"destination-details-fine-0031"},"indexTemplate":"source_question"},{"id":"source-question:ba9c1429d4b6f406016a298509274dd93dac6cad03e1bf986edea19eb95f6803","title":"This setting describes how a hidden source of supersymmetry breaking gravitationally affects a dark-energy scalar, even when the two superpotentials and the initial Kähler potential contain no direct cross terms.","connectionCount":1,"detail":{"shardId":"destination-details-fine-0031"},"indexTemplate":"source_question"},{"id":"source-question:ba3569ec28aa4aa5a210a602ecebd9be191cf458bf867885c4452571f90ad748","title":"The model provides self-gravitating scalar configurations on which to test conjectural field-range and potential-slope bounds. Equal-mass real scalars form a complex field with a radial, positive mass-plus-quartic potential.","connectionCount":1,"detail":{"shardId":"destination-details-fine-0036"},"indexTemplate":"source_question"},{"id":"source-question:bad22b78a74b1bef3b5dd8bcbf9b7d800b3050dfc4875dae017e4915d68caa23","title":"Can a supersymmetric massive-IIA AdS7 compactification with fixed flux and localized pole sources have continuous supersymmetry-breaking directions? The configurations have SO(3)-invariant profiles on an internal S3 and are studied in classical supergravity.","connectionCount":1,"detail":{"shardId":"destination-details-fine-0039"},"indexTemplate":"source_question"},{"id":"source-question:baf507e8ccc051349b69b07441405179f06034fa1b7de74da08f0d6e590d6600","title":"Does the reported bifurcation pattern persist in less symmetric higher-dimensional field spaces, and how should exact scaling backgrounds be used to calculate observable fluctuation correlations?","connectionCount":1,"detail":{"shardId":"destination-details-fine-0039"},"indexTemplate":"source_question"},{"id":"source-question:ba45822b31667bacac33f819d86d9181d0ad5e9114407e4a1e8f872a4f678fbe","title":"How does the conjectural trans-Planckian censorship constraint restrict warm inflation, and can two inflationary stages separated by radiation domination relax energy and tensor bounds while accommodating other swampland criteria?","connectionCount":1,"detail":{"shardId":"destination-details-fine-0046"},"indexTemplate":"source_question"},{"id":"source-question:ba2675931f239152b7f09da83d2b5679722a31510320b321023851372f6435b4","title":"Does the Hodge-theoretic attractor condition force algebraic moduli for Calabi–Yau varieties, as proposed in the higher-dimensional analogue of Moore's threefold Attractor Conjecture?","connectionCount":1,"detail":{"shardId":"destination-details-fine-0057"},"indexTemplate":"source_question"},{"id":"source-question:ba72cf37df0554976b85eddee32024723ad742155094a110a7c7e5b36efbbc74","title":"How does moduli stabilisation determine the flux-landscape distributions of closed-string axion decay constants, masses, dark matter abundance and gauge couplings, and how rare are intermediate-scale QCD axions?","connectionCount":1,"detail":{"shardId":"destination-details-fine-0065"},"indexTemplate":"source_question"},{"id":"source-question:baf2aa38f63d81357a05339a0c1969e63893d8ad15b7701e3421726cad0c66e7","title":"Does Festina Lente reasoning constrain how small non-abelian vector masses and confinement scales can be relative to the Hubble scale? The reviewed application addresses both types of scale, without specifying a particular gauge group or spectrum.","connectionCount":1,"detail":{"shardId":"destination-details-fine-0066"},"indexTemplate":"source_question"},{"id":"source-question:ba621645d41049bd2f53cf397a479818418b4fbb711433fe75a1fa7e1a9d8574","title":"In solutions driven by dynamical scalar tadpoles, does field-space distance distinguish spacetime-ending walls of nothing from interpolating domain walls, and how does the SDC scale relate to spacetime distance and curvature?","connectionCount":1,"detail":{"shardId":"destination-details-fine-0067"},"indexTemplate":"source_question"},{"id":"source-question:bae52b7aac32880bc5154659590a2995739c251486a871872836e0adcd5dfb87","title":"How do four-derivative corrections change the long-range static force between extremal black holes with massless scalars, and when do superextremality and self-repulsion impose different conditions?","connectionCount":1,"detail":{"shardId":"destination-details-fine-0069"},"indexTemplate":"source_question"},{"id":"source-question:ba2c4128f0492ba8c813024557bd15b2141884a861c386b8696eff83eabe315c","titl